{
  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "items": [
        "Carrier scale without the folklore: every rule that keeps carriers honest is a node or a gate here \u2014 premise-first intake, commit-before-verify, tiered blind review through a join, after_partial on the judges",
        "A complementary premise-gate pair routes dead questions to a stand-down terminal, so a blocked premise ends in a labeled record, never a silent drop",
        "The exit is a no-token machine gate: the run cannot go greener than the checkout snapshot it found, and a machine timeout is failure, not approval"
      ],
      "title": "Why it works"
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "items": [
        "18 nodes, 6 gates, 9 branches, 26 edges: intake -> premise pair -> build -> test -> fix -> judges -> review join -> PR | stand-down -> machine exit-check",
        "Review tiers itself on the diff-size line: sub-threshold diffs are single-reviewed and the join reads the skip as policy, not as loss",
        "Derived from this example's bytes by scripts/graph_diagram.py"
      ],
      "title": "Contract"
    }
  ],
